{
  "_comment": [
    "Design series, and the colloquial names people search by.",
    "",
    "'Series' is the industry's word, not one invented here: PCGS organises its",
    "price guide, population report and CoinFacts by series, so using the same",
    "term is what lets a coin be looked up against a published value.",
    "",
    "label is the formal name; aliases are what people actually say. That split",
    "is load-bearing rather than decorative. Measured against this collection's",
    "own descriptions: 'Mercury' appears 104 times and 'Winged Liberty Head'",
    "zero; 'Buffalo' 156 and 'Indian Head Nickel' zero; but 'Walking Liberty'",
    "130 against 'Walker' 2. Neither the formal names nor the nicknames alone",
    "would find everything.",
    "",
    "Only coin series are listed. US paper money is catalogued by Friedberg",
    "number rather than by design name, and its classes are already in",
    "note_type -- inventing a parallel currency-series vocabulary here would be",
    "exactly the made-up terminology this table exists to avoid.",
    "",
    "Dates are the years the design was struck. year_end is null for a series",
    "still in production."
  ],

